[["Map",1,2,45,46],"articles",["Map",3,4,19,20,32,33],"gods-saving-will-in-the-new-testament",{"id":3,"data":5,"filePath":17,"digest":18},{"title":6,"author":7,"issue":8,"published":9,"summary":10,"pdf":11,"tags":12},"God's Saving Will in the New Testament (1)","Rev. Angus Stewart","British Reformed Journal, Volume 77",["Date","2025-11-10T00:00:00.000Z"],"A study of the two Greek verbs for willing — thelō and boulomai — and how they appear throughout the New Testament to describe God's saving will. The author distinguishes God's will of decree (what He sovereignly decides) from His will of precept (what He commands), and traces the implications for assurance, prayer, and Christian living.","/articles/gods-saving-will-in-the-new-testament.pdf",[13,14,15,16],"Theology","Biblical Studies","Greek","Sovereignty","src/content/articles/gods-saving-will-in-the-new-testament.json","3f46f6534e122489","image-of-god-and-responsibility-of-man",{"id":19,"data":21,"filePath":30,"digest":31},{"title":22,"author":23,"issue":8,"published":24,"summary":25,"pdf":26,"tags":27},"The Image of God and the Responsibility of Man","Samuel Watterson",["Date","2025-11-10T00:00:00.000Z"],"Examining the Westminster Shorter Catechism's opening question in the light of Scripture, this article traces how God's purpose in creating man — to glorify Him and enjoy Him forever — is grounded in the creation of man in God's image and likeness. The author explores the implications of the image of God for the responsibility of all men, redeemed and unredeemed alike.","/articles/image-of-god-and-responsibility-of-man.pdf",[13,28,29],"Image of God","Westminster Standards","src/content/articles/image-of-god-and-responsibility-of-man.json","871344ddcdd55cd6","more-loving-than-god",{"id":32,"data":34,"filePath":43,"digest":44},{"title":35,"author":23,"issue":8,"published":36,"summary":37,"pdf":38,"tags":39},"Editorial: More Loving Than God? (3)",["Date","2025-11-10T00:00:00.000Z"],"The third in a series of editorials responding to the Open Theist challenge that God is less loving than those who wish all to be saved. The author turns from critique to construction, asking how Scripture itself measures God's love, and how that biblical measure shapes our calling to love both the elect and the ungodly.","/articles/more-loving-than-god.pdf",[40,13,41,42],"Editorial","Open Theism","Love of God","src/content/articles/more-loving-than-god.json","f1862b1bb3d0d204","meta::meta",["Map",47,48,49,50,51,52],"astro-config-digest","{\"root\":{},\"srcDir\":{},\"publicDir\":{},\"outDir\":{},\"cacheDir\":{},\"compressHTML\":\"jsx\",\"base\":\"/\",\"trailingSlash\":\"ignore\",\"output\":\"static\",\"scopedStyleStrategy\":\"attribute\",\"build\":{\"format\":\"directory\",\"client\":{},\"server\":{},\"assets\":\"_astro\",\"serverEntry\":\"entry.mjs\",\"redirects\":true,\"inlineStylesheets\":\"auto\",\"concurrency\":1},\"server\":{\"open\":false,\"host\":\"127.0.0.1\",\"port\":4321,\"allowedHosts\":[\"127.0.0.1\",\"127.0.0.1\",\"127.0.0.1\",\"127.0.0.1\"]},\"redirects\":{},\"image\":{\"endpoint\":{\"route\":\"/_image\"},\"service\":{\"entrypoint\":\"astro/assets/services/sharp\",\"config\":{}},\"dangerouslyProcessSVG\":false,\"domains\":[],\"remotePatterns\":[],\"responsiveStyles\":false},\"devToolbar\":{\"enabled\":true},\"markdown\":{\"syntaxHighlight\":{\"type\":\"shiki\",\"excludeLangs\":[\"math\"]},\"shikiConfig\":{\"langs\":[],\"langAlias\":{},\"theme\":\"github-dark\",\"themes\":{},\"wrap\":false,\"transformers\":[]},\"remarkPlugins\":[],\"rehypePlugins\":[],\"remarkRehype\":{},\"processor\":{\"name\":\"satteri\",\"options\":{\"mdastPlugins\":[],\"hastPlugins\":[],\"features\":{}}}},\"security\":{\"checkOrigin\":true,\"allowedDomains\":[],\"csp\":false,\"actionBodySizeLimit\":1048576,\"serverIslandBodySizeLimit\":1048576},\"env\":{\"schema\":{},\"validateSecrets\":false},\"prerenderConflictBehavior\":\"warn\",\"fetchFile\":\"fetch\",\"experimental\":{\"clientPrerender\":false,\"contentInte